The weird thing about that was that she brought her

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.943
eighteen year-old daughter and she was like, 45 years-old.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.170
And she brought her daughter as moral support.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.090
- I'd have the say the most awkward for me

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.423
was tattooing a gentleman's cock.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.243
It turned literally the entire thing, from tip to balls,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.193
into a snake, it was surreal.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.820
- I absolutely hate it when I'm sitting in the shop

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.920
and a client walks in and they have no idea

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.753
what they wanna get.

00:01:28.753 --> 00:01:29.650
- They tell us we can do whatever we want

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.470
and then we start drawing stuff up

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.540
and it's never what they want, so that makes no sense to us.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.740
- Nobody ever really means do what you want,

00:01:37.516 --> 00:01:39.040
what they mean is do what they want,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.290
as long as you can figure it out,

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.853
which is next to impossible.

00:01:42.907 --> 00:01:45.557
- "I need a tattoo, what do you think I should get?

00:01:45.557 --> 00:01:48.777
"Oh, by the way, my flight leaves in three hours."

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.017
- Getting a tattoo does hurt.

00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:54.800
Whoever doesn't say it doesn't hurt, they're a little weird.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.840
But, you know, everyone takes pain differently.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.380
- It's not terrible.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.910
It's not as bad as people think.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.113
It's all about your state of mind, honestly.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.635
- Everybody's different.

00:02:04.635 --> 00:02:07.990
Literally, like where I think the most painful spot

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.990
on the body is, which would be like ribs or lower back,

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.820
for me personally, I tattoo people all day

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.270
that sit like that's nothing.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.410
(laughing)

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.553
- Of course!

00:02:19.749 --> 00:02:20.790
Yeah.
(off-camera laughter)

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:21.623
Who doesn't?

00:02:21.623 --> 00:02:22.456
Who wouldn't?

00:02:22.456 --> 00:02:23.400
- As a professional,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.163
I'm supposed to be objective and not judge people.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:27.940
However, as a human,

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.120
I judge everybody that walks through the door.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.190
- As artists we have to, you know,

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:34.350
give them what they want.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.470
We're just gonna give you a good piece.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.073
We want you to walk out with a great piece.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.010
If you come in with an idea,

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.250
you're going to an artist that you like their style,

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.650
and if you like their work

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:44.790
then you're gonna get something really good.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.620
- I think if the tattoo is composed really well

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.603
and it's a very dynamic tattoo,

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:53.320
as an artist I think that makes for a really great tattoo.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.340
For as far as a client goes, my end goal

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.670
is to have a client leave with a smile on their face.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.620
If they're happy, and they love what I did,

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:01.620
then that's perfect.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.010
- I'd say before you get a tattoo,

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.540
you definitely need to think about it.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:10.300
Look for artists that you like

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.600
so that you know what style you're looking for.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.950
- At this day and age, if you get a bad tattoo,

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.810
you kinda deserve it.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:18.590
It's because you didn't do the research.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.320
- A lot of people get, like, small tattoos to start off,

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.163
to feel the pain and all that.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.823
I always say don't do that.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.720
If you want something big, get it big.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.350
- And don't be a stickler about money.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:33.680
We put years into our craft and we're worth what we ask for.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.883
Good tattoos aren't cheap and cheap tattoos aren't good.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.190
If you know somebody that can do it in their garage,

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.180
by all means go get it,

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.433
but I'm gonna charge you a lot to fix it.

00:03:43.705 --> 00:03:46.288
(upbeat music)

